WEBVTT

00:01:56.445 --> 00:02:00.825
they believe in not just studying cultures
that we already know that are familiar

00:02:00.825 --> 00:02:04.412
but cultures which are unfamiliar.

00:02:04.453 --> 00:02:06.998
That can be on the other
side of the world,

00:02:06.998 --> 00:02:09.000
it can be down the end of the street,

00:02:09.041 --> 00:02:10.543
a different profession,

00:02:10.543 --> 00:02:13.796
or, shock horror,
a different political party.

00:02:14.172 --> 00:02:15.423
(Laughter)

00:02:15.423 --> 00:02:18.384
And anthropologists do this
for two reasons.

00:02:18.885 --> 00:02:21.179
Firstly, understanding people

00:02:21.179 --> 00:02:23.764
who have a different point of view to you

00:02:23.806 --> 00:02:26.642
is very helpful for making
sense of the world.

00:02:26.684 --> 00:02:27.894
Duh.

00:02:27.894 --> 00:02:30.062
It's something we ought to all know,